── CHANGING A LIST WHILE READING IT ── E0404_changing_a_list_while_reading_it.lt:1:57  [E0404]

`orders` is being read by a `for` loop around this change:

  1 │ fn doubled(inout orders: List<i64>) { for o in orders { orders.push(o) } }
    │                                                         ^^^^^^

Changing a list while a `for` loop reads it would silently copy it. Build the
changes in another list and apply them after the loop, or loop over its indexes.
